# Tracer: template trust-have uses the common strict rejection gate.
# Before (wrongly accepted under -strict):
# template<S set>:
#     trust have template_assumed R:
#         template_assumed = 1
# Former behavior: exit 0 under -strict because only the outer template was checked.
#
# Now: this source stays legal in an ordinary run; -strict rejects it before
# introducing template parameters or storing the definition.
template<S set>:
    trust have template_assumed R:
        template_assumed = 1

# Boundary: ordinary checked templates still pass strict; user axioms also
# require ordinary mode and cannot bypass the strict gate in proof bodies.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -lang en -f examples/stmt_nodes/unsafe/template_strict_policy.lit
# Rejection: same command with -strict exits 1 with forbidden trust-have.
# Tests: execute::statement_boundary_tests::strict_rejects_template_trust_at_top_level_and_in_proof_bodies.
